            <div xml:id="d530">

                <pb facs="0605" n="539" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg539"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/7955: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-02-26T17:00:00-05:45">February 26, 1934—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>73. General Somoza has just telephoned me that commander of central area has
                    communicated by radio that many Sandinistas have <pb facs="0606" n="540"
                        xml:id="pg540"/> voluntarily surrendered in operations in vicinity of Wiwili
                    requesting to be incorporated in Guardia but are without food and shelter.
                    Somoza stated that he had instructed commander to provide food and lodging.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
